xpression. It is typical of the confusion of terminology in early chemistry that the London Pharmacopoeia of 1721 gave the name Spiritus Veneris to sulphuric acid obtained by the distillation of copper sulphate.", "reference": "2004, Maurice P. Crosland, Historical Studies in the Language of Chemistry, page 89:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "af", "name": "Afrikaans"}, "word": "spiritus"}, {"language": {"code": "ar", "name": "Arabic"}, "word": "كُحُول"}, {"language": {"code": "hy", "name": "Armenian"}, "word": "սպիրտ"}, {"language": {"code": "be", "name": "Belarusian"}, "word": "алкаго́ль"}, {"language": {"code": "be", "name": "Belarusian"}, "word": "спірт"}, {"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "алкохо́л"}, {"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "спирт"}, {"language": {"code": "cmn", "name": "Chinese Mandarin"}, "word": "酒"}, {"language": {"code": "cs", "name": "Czech"}, "word": "líh"}, {"language": {"code": "da", "name": "Danish"}, "word": "spiritus"}, {"language": {"code": "da", "name": "Danish"}, "word": "sprit"}, {"language": {"code": "da", "name": "Danish"}, "word": "alkohol"}, {"language": {"code": "eo", "name": "Esperanto"}, "word": "alkoholaĵo"}, {"language": {"code": "et", "name": "Estonian"}, "word": "viin"}, {"language": {"code": "et", "name": "Estonian"}, "word": "piiritus"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "alkoholi"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "viina"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "pirtu"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "sprii"}, {"language": {"code": "fr", "name": "French"}, "word": "spiritueux"}, {"language": {"code": "ka", "name": "Georgian"}, "word": "სპირტი"}, {"language": {"code": "de", "name": "German"}, "word": "Schnaps"}, {"language": {"code": "de", "name": "German"}, "word": "Sprit"}, {"language": {"code": "de", "name": "German"}, "word": "Alkohol"}, {"